          "label": "<p>On immunohistochemistry, an invasive breast carcinoma is oestrogen-receptor nega</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>On immunohistochemistry, an invasive breast carcinoma is oestrogen-receptor negative, progesterone-receptor negative and HER2 2+. What is the appropriate next step?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>Report it as HER2-positive and start trastuzumab</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A 2+ score is equivocal, not positive. Trastuzumab eligibility needs confirmed gene amplification, not the IHC score alone.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Report it as triple-negative carcinoma</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Triple-negative status requires HER2 to be truly negative. An equivocal 2+ result cannot be called negative until amplification has been excluded.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Confirm HER2 gene amplification by fluorescence in situ hybridisation (FISH)</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>A 2+ score is resolved by FISH. A ratio above 2.0, or more than six gene copies per cell, confirms amplification. It would make the tumour HER2-enriched and eligible for trastuzumab.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>Add endocrine therapy as for Luminal A disease</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Endocrine therapy works only in oestrogen-receptor-positive tumours, and Luminal A is ER-positive with low Ki-67. This tumour is ER-negative.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "HER2 2+ on IHC is equivocal. FISH confirms amplification (ratio above 2.0, or more than six copies per cell). Only then can the subtype and trastuzumab eligibility be decided."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct. HER2 2+ is equivocal, and FISH decides whether the tumour is HER2-enriched or triple-negative."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
